{"book":10,"chapter":10,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / RUST AFTER PYTHON / CHAPTER 10","slides":[{"title":"From def to fn","sub":"Chapter 10 · Python → Rust","short":"Intro","main":"Braces instead of indentation; elif → else if; where Python's freedom ends.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["def → fn","Braces instead of indentation","What gets replaced"],"captions":["Most Python code translates to Rust almost one to one","Colon and indentation → curly braces; elif → else if","Where Python gives freedom and Rust does not — we'll see what replaces it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"def f(a):","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"fn f(a: i32) -> i32","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["if x > 0:","    y = 1","elif x < 0:","    y = -1"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":160.0},{"t":"code","id":"d","x":190.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["if x > 0 {","    y = 1","} else if x < 0 {","    y = -1","}"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":160.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"arguments","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"*args","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"yield","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"try","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.0,23.2]}]},{"title":"Signatures","sub":"Types are mandatory","short":"Signatures","main":"Python annotations are not checked; in Rust types are mandatory; generics.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python","Rust","Generics"],"captions":["def add(a, b): — types are optional; the interpreter does not check annotations","fn add(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 — types are mandatory, checked on every call","Universal code goes through generics: fn add<T: Add>(a: T, b: T) -> T"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def add(a, b):","    return a + b","add(1, 2); add(\"a\", \"b\")"],"lang":"rust","size":11.5,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn add(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 {","    a + b","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn add<T: std::ops::Add<Output = T>>(","    a: T, b: T) -> T {","    a + b","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[10.9,24.2]}]},{"title":"Default values","sub":"Option and builder","short":"Default","main":"No default: Option, two functions, a builder struct.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No default","Option","Builder"],"captions":["def hi(name=\"world\"): — not possible in Rust: no default values and no named parameters","Take Option<&str> and substitute unwrap_or(\"world\"), or write two functions","Collect the parameters into a struct with defaults — the “builder” pattern"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def hi(name=\"world\"): ...","// fn hi(name = \"world\")  ✕"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn hi(name: Option<&str>) {","    let n = name.unwrap_or(\"world\");","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["Config::default()","    .name(\"Anya\")","    .retries(3)","    .build()"],"lang":"rust","size":11.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.0,23.8]}]},{"title":"*args and **kwargs","sub":"Slices and structs","short":"*args","main":"A slice instead of *args; a struct instead of **kwargs.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["*args → slice","Different types","**kwargs"],"captions":["*args → a slice parameter: fn total(v: &[i32]) — pass an array or a vector","Values of different types — a struct or an enum","**kwargs → a struct with fields or a HashMap; macros (println!) take any number of arguments"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def total(*args): ...","fn total(v: &[i32]) -> i32"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"(1, \"a\", 2.5)","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"struct / enum","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"**kwargs","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"struct Options { … }","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.1,28.7]}]},{"title":"Returning values","sub":"Tuple, (), Option, Result","short":"Returns","main":"Tuple, () instead of None, Option and Result.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["As a tuple","None → ()","Option and Result"],"captions":["return a, b → fn f() -> (i32, i32) { (a, b) }; the result is the last expression","No return → None; in Rust with no arrow, () is returned","The value may be missing — Option<T>; the operation may fail — Result<T, E>"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["return a, b","(a, b)   // Rust: the last expression"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"None","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"()","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Option<T>\nno value","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Result<T, E>\nerror","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[7.5,25.4]}]},{"title":"Functions as values","sub":"fn and closures","short":"Closures","main":"Function pointer and |x| x + 1.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Function pointer","Closure","Passing"],"captions":["An ordinary function is passed by name; its type is fn(i32) -> i32","lambda x: x + 1 → |x| x + 1: a closure can capture variables","apply(f, 5) — a function takes another function; details in the iterators chapter"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn inc(x: i32) -> i32 { x + 1 }","let f: fn(i32) -> i32 = inc;"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let f = |x| x + 1;","let k = 10;","let g = |x| x + k;   // capture"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn apply(f: fn(i32) -> i32, x: i32) -> i32 {","    f(x)","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[11.2,31.8]}]},{"title":"Documentation","sub":"/// and doctest","short":"Docs","main":"/// and cargo doc; examples run as tests.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["docstring","///","Doctest"],"captions":["Python: a triple-quoted string right after def","Rust: /// before the function, Markdown markup; cargo doc builds a docs site","A code example in a comment runs as a test (cargo test) — the docs never go stale"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["def f(x):","    \"\"\"Doubles x.\"\"\""],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["/// Doubles the number.","fn double(x: i32) -> i32 {","    x * 2","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["/// ```","/// assert_eq!(double(2), 4);","/// ```"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[9.2,29.6]}]},{"title":"Conditions","sub":"if, else if, &&, ||, !","short":"Conditions","main":"Only bool; &&, ||, !; no ternary operator.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["if / else if","Only bool","and, or, not"],"captions":["if / elif / else → if / else if / else; no parentheses around the condition","if lst: and if not x: are not allowed — compare explicitly: if !v.is_empty()","and, or, not → &&, ||, !; x if c else y → if c { x } else { y }; in → contains"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"elif","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"else if","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"if lst:","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"if !v.is_empty()","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["a and not b   →   a && !b","x in v          →   v.contains(&x)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.1,25.1]}]},{"title":"match","sub":"Chains and patterns","short":"match","main":"No 1 < x < 10 chain; match with ranges and guards.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Chain 1 < x < 10","match","Guards"],"captions":["No comparison chains: write x > 1 && x < 10 or (2..10).contains(&x)","Python 3.10 match-case → match: ranges, |, struct destructuring, all cases required","Guard: Some(n) if n > 0 => … — an extra condition in the arm"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["1 < x < 10          # Python","x > 1 && x < 10   // Rust","(2..10).contains(&x)"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["match n {","    0 => \"zero\",","    1 | 2 => \"few\",","    3..=9 => \"medium\",","    _ => \"many\",","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["match x {","    Some(n) if n > 0 => \"positive\",","    Some(_) => \"not positive\",","    None => \"none\",","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[17.7,31.2]}]},{"title":"Loops","sub":"range, while, loop","short":"Loops","main":"0..n, loop instead of while True, no for-else.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["range","while and loop","No for-else"],"captions":["for i in range(n) → for i in 0..n; step — step_by, reverse — rev(); enumerate and zip exist","while → while; while True → loop; break can return a value; labels exit nested loops","A loop has no else branch: write a search with a flag or with find and any"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for i in range(n):        for i in 0..n {","for i in range(10, 0, -1): for i in (1..=10).rev()"],"lang":"rust","size":7.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"while True:","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"loop { … }","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let found = v.iter().any(|&x| x == 7);","let pos = v.iter().position(|&x| x == 7);"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[9.7,26.4]}]},{"title":"Errors","sub":"Result instead of exceptions","short":"Errors","main":"Result, the ? operator, panic!.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No exceptions","?","panic!"],"captions":["try / except → Result: the function itself states a possible error in its type","The ? operator passes the error up — like raise, but visible in the signature","panic! — for the unrecoverable (raise with no catch); assert! — condition checks"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"try:\n    … except","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"match / ?\non Result","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn read() -> Result<i32, ParseIntError> {","    let n = \"5\".parse::<i32>()?;","    Ok(n)","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"raise Exception","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"panic!(\"…\")","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[17.1,25.1]}]},{"title":"Generators","sub":"Iterators and chains","short":"Iterators","main":"yield → Iterator; comprehensions → chains; any and all.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["yield → Iterator","Comprehension","any and all"],"captions":["Python generators → Rust iterators: anything with next() works in for and in chains","[x*2 for x in v if x > 0] → v.iter().filter(…).map(…).collect()","any(…) and all(…) → the iterator methods any and all; the chain compiles to a plain loop"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"yield x","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"impl Iterator\nfn next()","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let r: Vec<i32> = v.iter()","    .filter(|x| **x > 0)","    .map(|x| x * 2)","    .collect();"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["v.iter().any(|&x| x > 9)","v.iter().all(|&x| x > 0)"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[17.2,25.4]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: strings.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Cheat sheet","Next"],"captions":["def → fn; types are mandatory; no default and *args; the result is the last expression","if and match are expressions; no comparison chains or for-else; no exceptions; generators → iterators","Next chapter — strings: str from Python and String with &str from Rust"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"fn","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"types","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"match","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Result","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["fn f(x: i32) -> Option<i32> {","    if x > 0 { Some(x) } else { None }","}"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":240.0,"h":34.0,"text":"str ↔ String / &str","tone":"blue","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.5,25.3]}]}]}